<Vertical id="FreewriteDemo" title="Freewrite Block Demo">

  <Markdown id="intro">
## Freewriting Exercises

Freewriting is a technique where you write continuously without stopping,
editing, or worrying about quality. These demos show different constraint
combinations.

### 1. Full freewrite

You can't see what you're writing and you can't go back. Just write.
  </Markdown>

  <TimedContainer id="t1" duration="2 minutes" hideuntilstart="true"
                  before="Write whatever comes to mind. Don't stop.">
    <Freewrite id="fw1" invisible="true" nodelete="true"
               counter="true" pace="true" />
  </TimedContainer>

  <Markdown id="desc2">
### 2. No-delete mode

You can see your text, but you can't edit it.
  </Markdown>

  <TimedContainer id="t2" duration="1 minute" hideuntilstart="true"
                  before="Write continuously for one minute.">
    <Freewrite id="fw2" nodelete="true" counter="true" />
  </TimedContainer>

  <Markdown id="desc3">
### 3. Invisible mode

You can't see what you're writing, but backspace works if you need it.
  </Markdown>

  <TimedContainer id="t3" duration="90 seconds" hideuntilstart="true"
                  before="Write without seeing your words.">
    <Freewrite id="fw3" invisible="true" counter="true" pace="true" />
  </TimedContainer>

  <Markdown id="desc4">
### 4. Timed writing

Just a timed writing session with word count.
  </Markdown>

  <TimedContainer id="t4" duration="3 minutes" hideuntilstart="true"
                  before="Free writing time.">
    <Freewrite id="fw4" counter="true" rows="12" />
  </TimedContainer>

</Vertical>
